{
  "about": "Every one of the CLI's 61 command names with --json (rust/PLAN-CORE-PORT.md section 11, C0: the --json fixtures for all 48 commands), over a registry with one stopped server: the envelope each answers with, the INVALID_USAGE error for those that take no --json, and the data of those that do. test/cli-json-coverage.test.mjs fails when mcctl.mjs gains a command this scenario does not run. The golden file test/fixtures/contracts/cli/cli-json.json holds the Node answers; steps whose answer depends on the machine (doctor, repair, metrics, diag, backup sizes) are compared between the sides but kept out of it.",
  "golden": "test/fixtures/contracts/cli/cli-json.json",
  "goldenAbout": "What the Node core prints for every command name with --json (tools/parity/scenarios/cli-json.json). Each ported command must print the same envelope. Regenerate with node tools/parity/run.mjs tools/parity/scenarios/cli-json.json --update-golden; a change here changes the CLI's --json contract (schemaVersion 1).",
